A||||10||Bluebottlejunky||Turtle Wax good or bad?||||1||
Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||04-14-2001||11:23 PM||||Im sure everyone here has there own idea on turtle wax..but I was looking at some of there products like Color Back that says it renews and gets rid of oxidation n the car.  Has anyone ever used it befor?  I have never used turtle wax befor only armorall.<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||04-14-2001||11:29 PM||||If it is the "colored" wax, it is bad. It only lasts a few days then it starts fading in blotches. Also the car will look funny on a hot sunny day if you don't get an even coat. <BR>Try the Meguire's 3-step system, It will remove light to medium oxidation and will make the car look like glass.||||reg||13
Z||000002||FieroJoe||04-14-2001||11:31 PM||||I assume that you are trying to get rid of the dead layer of oxidized clear coat that is found on many older cars.  I personally would just use a buffing compound with a high speed buffer and then polish it (also high speed).  If you dont want to go through all that, try one of the clay bar treatments, Mother's makes a kit that should restore your paint to shineyness!<P>edit:  I second that on the colored wax.  The only thing it is good at doing is staining things.  Dosent even work worth a damn at filling in scratches, and even worse at being a wax.<BR>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroJoe (edited 04-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bluebottlejunky||04-15-2001||12:24 AM||||cool thanks alot guys..no turtle wax for me!||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||04-15-2001||11:22 AM||||I use Turtle Wax Swirl Remover/polish on my cars and it works fine. Its just all these different MIRACLE WAXES that are no good. Everyone including Turtle Wax makes them. Ive known people that use some of those lifetime waxes from tv ads and ruined thier paint jobs.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||2M4 Dale||04-15-2001||04:02 PM||||I've found that any wax that is hard to put on and harder to take off is the best......the quickie on-off stuff don't last. I use Turtle Wax looks great stays a long time.||||reg||6
Z||000006||grinthock||04-15-2001||04:05 PM||||For more info see my other thread<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006875.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006875.html</A> <P>It's got some info on wax and stuff  ||||reg||3
Z||000007||saleenfiero||04-15-2001||05:37 PM||||As if Turtle Wax doesn't have anything wrong with it.  I just put it on the other day and it looks great.  I would never buy another kind of wax (um, unless of course it was on sale like turtle wax was!)<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||2
Z||000008||Old Lar||04-15-2001||07:12 PM||||There are cleaners and there are cleaner/waxes.  Macguires has cleaners and waxes.  Turtle wax is a cleaner wax.  Macquires is a two step product, Turtle wax is a one step product.  I've used both and they al look good.  I have gone as far a putting down a layer of pure carnuba wax and polishing that up after cleaning and waxing.  It makes for a deep shine. And if you have a day to spend cleaning, waxing, polishing etc.||||reg||3
Z||000009||Cameron||04-15-2001||07:13 PM||||Everybody has had good and bad things to say about every type of wax.  Personally I have heard more bad things about Turtle Wax then good so I avoid the stuff.||||reg||3
Z||000010||deceler8||04-16-2001||10:17 AM||||I've probably used near everything in the past 25 years and I keep coming back to J-Wax Kit.<P>The Kit paste is the best paste wax I've ever used and the Kit liquid is the best liquid I've ever used. Easy to apply, easy to remove, nice carnauba shine and the price doesn't break you.<P>And available nearly everywhere.||||reg||1
